{
  "cell": "ro_buf",
  "_comment": [
    "Cell descriptor for layout/bin/compose-cell.py -- see layout/README.md",
    "section 'Composing a gate' for the floorplan reasoning behind every",
    "number here, and layout/ro_buf/README.md for this cell's own result.",
    "",
    "ro_buf is design/ro_array_core.spice's unstarved CMOS inverter (the",
    "per-ring output buffer): XMp 0.84/0.15 pfet + XMn 0.42/0.15 nfet, with",
    "PMOS bulk on vdd and NMOS bulk on vss.",
    "",
    "Placement is a two-row stack: NMOS at the origin, PMOS mirrored in y",
    "directly above it so the two gates face each other, with a tap island to",
    "the west of each row supplying that row's body tie. Origins are chosen so",
    "that (a) the nwell tap island's own nwell OVERLAPS the PMOS block's nwell",
    "by 0.10 um -- merging them into one electrical node -- while their li1",
    "stays 0.20 um apart (sky130 li1 spacing floor is 0.17 um), and (b) every",
    "routed net is a straight or single-jog run that clears both endpoint",
    "blocks' interiors."
  ],
  "pdk": {
    "variant": "sky130A",
    "deck": "sky130"
  },
  "blocks": [
    {
      "id": "mn",
      "generator": "mos_array",
      "cell_name": "nfet_w0p42_l0p15",
      "orientation": "none",
      "params": {
        "w_um": 0.42,
        "l_um": 0.15,
        "rows": 1,
        "cols": 1,
        "dummy": 0,
